id: pm-beads-tma4
title: Resume bounded Beads transfers with dependency closure and chunk receipts
description: "Add a dependency-aware transfer plan and resumable per-chunk application using public pm SDK capabilities. Overlap checked against the current CLI, pm-beads and pm-context: keep existing JSONL parser, structural validation and core transactions; do not duplicate neighborhood packing."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-beads#165"
created_at: "2026-10-24T11:13:36.736Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T17:03:01.005Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "A killed transfer resumes without duplicates; A late cross-chunk dependency is resolved without dangling edges; Exceeding closure limits yields an explicit omission or refusal receipt; Concurrent drainers inspect and mutate state under the SDK writer lease; foreign records are skipped with reasons; all transition boundaries have interleaving tests on one non-git tracker; Typed SDK and CLI, bounded TOON/JSON receipts, README and example, public tracker copy measurements, and npm plus Bun CI release gates"
comments[31]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-24T11:13:52.625Z",codex-agent,"Overlap audit: registry confirms CLI 2026.10.24; this package retains its 2026.10.20 SDK pin. Existing Beads validation handles structural errors, cycles and aliases; existing import batches delegate core mutations. Core SDK exports commitItemMutations and commitWorkspaceTransaction with resumable journals; pm-context provides bounded neighborhood/delta packs, not a transfer ledger. Add only closure planning, immutable transfer identities and per-chunk receipts around those public coordinators. Use non-git trackers and deterministic interleaving at every package/coordinator transition."
  "2026-10-24T11:20:04.804Z",codex-agent,"Design refinement: dependency-first creation includes parent closure, so every published edge targets an earlier owned row even when its source record appears later or crosses chunks. The SDK transaction journal itself is the per-chunk checkpoint; no second mutable checkpoint store. Ownership comes from immutable create history, not copied bead_id markers. Skip foreign identities and their unavailable dependents, preserve peer edits, and never delete or close progress during compensation. The pinned bulk-create helper adopts any occupied id, so ownership-aware steps use commitWorkspaceTransaction plus PmClient.create instead."
  "2026-10-24T11:29:18.808Z",codex-agent,"Verification: linked command node --test test/transfer.test.ts test/transfer-cli.test.ts passed 11/11, zero skips, including an actual SIGKILL after durable creation and recovery after the SDK lease TTL. Same-tracker interleavings cover all 9 forward coordinator boundaries, all 8 compensation boundaries, both create boundaries and competing drainers before acquisition. New transfer module targeted V8 coverage: 100% lines/branches/functions. Existing smoke and flag tests: 117/117. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint pass; this repository has no separate lint script."
  "2026-10-24T11:29:19.863Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replacing only buildPlan closure/order with selected-row-only batching makes both closure and cross-chunk drain regressions fail (0/2). Replacing only foreign ownership inspection with occupied-id adoption makes the foreign-record regression fail (0/1). Production source restored byte-for-byte, sha256 f427f51ed3407ffb07405f641126dd2eb8ef0bd581cfa4d625a6b05864017832; targeted suite passes after restoration."
  "2026-10-24T11:29:20.976Z",codex-agent,"Public real-data validation: read-only archived unbraind/pm-context tracker at c484938837a10e2b0963300d604c748e5c22f5f9, tracker tree d59e3c27dbd17ddbe71a0e5e1f1247321c74f6a6. Certified 89 rows, 58720 input bytes; all 89 transferred in 6 chunks with one real dependency edge, 0 duplicates/skips/dangling edges, 6 replayed chunks, and explicit maxRows/maxBytes refusals. Canonical plan 62173 bytes; compact JSON plan/resume receipts 712/3114 bytes. Separate public pm-beads run: 98 rows, 7 chunks, 8 parent links, 0 dependency edges, 0 duplicates/skips/dangling edges. Both archived copies stayed hash-identical and read-only; sources unchanged; execution used no git on PATH in non-git scratch trackers."
  "2026-10-24T11:29:22.066Z",codex-agent,"Operational boundary: this is creation-only exchange, not merging existing identities. Use reconciliation for incoming updates. Exact plans and SDK journals must be retained to resume; changed payloads or bounds create separate exchanges. A killed process may leave the core 30-second lease until expiry; busy is a typed retry receipt. Public SDK pin stays unchanged. Linked-test results are reported but tracker test-result persistence is disabled by existing project policy; results are recorded here. Full npm and Bun release gates are delegated to CI to avoid saturating the host."
  "2026-10-24T11:32:12.647Z",codex-agent,"Final ownership audit found a lifecycle interleaving worth testing: a peer can delete and recreate the same core id while history remains append-only. Ownership now uses the most recent create operation rather than the first, so a foreign replacement cannot inherit an earlier transfer creation marker. Added the same-tracker regression; foreign replacements and dependents skip without modifying the replacement."
  "2026-10-24T11:33:11.118Z",codex-agent,"Lifecycle experiment clarification: the public core correctly refuses recreating an identity with retained history (item_identity_reserved). No history was rewritten. The added regression instead uses an actual foreign create/delete tombstone: transfer now reads retained history even when its document is absent and skips that reserved identity and its dependent with reasons. This prevents a generic reserved-id failure and preserves peer deletion. Ownership also checks the latest creation record for defensive compatibility; source inspection failures classify the occupied identity as foreign."
  "2026-10-24T11:34:55.072Z",codex-agent,"Final local verification after the reserved-history guard: linked transfer tests pass 12/12 with zero skips, including SIGKILL and foreign tombstones. Targeted transfer.ts coverage remains 100% lines/branches/functions. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint pass. Reverting only the missing-document retained-history classification makes the new tombstone regression fail; production source restored byte-for-byte at sha256 2926d8a94801efeae21688b25234c8ec4f09f6ac22a84a5f2c8dca06b730e875. Both public tracker-copy measurements were repeated unchanged: 89/6/1 dependency and 98/7/8 parents, zero duplicates/skips/dangling edges. PR 165 is ready for review; waiting for npm and Bun CI gates on the final commit, without merge or release."
  "2026-10-24T12:55:10.990Z",codex-agent,"Review round: audit all importer mutation paths against pinned SDK typings and runtime defaults; explicitly isolate source fields from focus, templates, assignment, tags, workflow and author context. Add real non-git tracker full-document regressions, behavioral revert proof and release-gate evidence."
  "2026-10-24T13:00:25.024Z",codex-agent,"SDK audit: PmClient.create dispatches runCreate, whose inheritFocusedParent reads saved tracker focus whenever parent is absent and unset lacks parent. The typed SharedLinkedResourceClearOptions.unset supports explicit clearing; CreateResult documents parent_source=focus but the create typings do not explain unset parent as the focus opt-out. Templates apply only when template is supplied (omission disables); no standalone default-tags/default-assignee settings exist in this pin. Configured template fields, governance create_default_type/create_mode_default, per-type default_status, hardcoded priority fallback and author fallback are covered by source-explicit values. Update/link/close/restore do not inherit create defaults and must retain unrelated local fields; their author is now explicit. Transfer ownership accepts the SDK audit suffix appended by explicit unsets."
  "2026-10-24T13:06:47.370Z",codex-agent,"Full-document ambient regressions pass for transfer, reconciliation create/update/links, legacy import/upsert/close, and reconciliation restore/close compensation. Real receiver controls prove saved focus, template tags/assignee, default Issue type, per-Task blocked status and extension field defaults are active. Imported mutations disable extensions through typed noExtensions or --no-extensions; no SDK mocks. The recorded six-file linked targeted command passed 94/94, zero failures/skips; two legacy argv assertions were updated to account for explicit quoted edge authors. Local typecheck, build:test and docstring lint pass."
  "2026-10-24T13:08:02.287Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: removed only parent from the SDK unset filter and --unset parent from legacy creation; retained every other fix and all tests, then rebuilt. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"transfer ignores|reconciliation create|legacy importer\" test/ambient-defaults.test.ts failed 3/3 (exit 1), each full-document diff showing the extra focused parent. Restored mutation.ts and index.ts byte-for-byte (SHA256 551136530afb226d5466358ded42fb3bcef56066936100753a13226fcd2d8342 and 3b95af1d4a18dfef5d8d127deda71dca0fb4700a0bb28dd797d8a7d5a44240c8), rebuilt, and node --test test/ambient-defaults.test.ts passed 6/6, zero failures/skips. No history records were rewritten."
  "2026-10-24T13:09:15.404Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof is recorded above. The final local checks pass: typecheck, build:test, docstring lint (91/91 declarations across 12 files) and whitespace validation. Stock local health reports pre-existing merge-fence drift plus an ignored local pm-github version skew; linked to the existing pm-beads-v9r1 follow-up. No pin bump, history repair, or unrelated generated fence change is included. CI performs fresh installation and supplies full npm/Bun release and tracker-health evidence."
  "2026-10-24T13:09:28.089Z",codex-agent,"Final linked targeted run after the author resolver and creation-boundary assertion: node --test test/ambient-defaults.test.ts test/transfer.test.ts test/transfer-cli.test.ts test/reconcile.test.ts test/reconcile-cli.test.ts test/import-paths.test.ts passed 95/95, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, via pm test --run --only-last --progress. Local build, typecheck, build:test, docstring lint and whitespace checks pass. Implementation and revert proof are ready for exact-head CI verification; keep this item in_progress for the orchestrator."
  "2026-10-24T13:13:00.325Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40096973144 on b842e15 passed 453/453 tests on Node 22 and 26 and passed fresh tracker health, but npm release:check correctly failed its unchanged 100% coverage threshold: aggregate branches 99.89%, index.ts 99.75%. mutation.ts, transfer.ts and reconciliation remain 100% lines/branches/functions. Investigating the missing legacy-import branch before repushing; Bun gate has not run and is not counted as evidence."
  "2026-10-24T13:25:35.699Z",codex-agent,"CI coverage debugging: local pinned Node 26 coverage wrapper with isolated HOME and git config passes all 453 tests and 100% lines/branches/functions across 12 sources, while CI reports two uncovered index.ts branches. Added a failure-only CI LCOV branch-location diagnostic so the exact missing paths are inspectable; gate scope and thresholds remain unchanged. Earlier overlapping diagnostic gate attempts were discarded; only the serial pinned coverage run is evidence."
  "2026-10-24T13:29:20.681Z",codex-agent,"CI 40098096900 on 7413388 passes 453/453 and 100% lines/branches/functions across 12 sources on both Node versions, without changing importer code from b842e15. The release attestation scanner then rejected dollar signs inside the failure-only JavaScript heredoc (regex anchor and template literal) as shell expansions. Rewrote the diagnostic without dollar signs; npm run verify:release-publish-attestation now passes locally. No thresholds, measured source scope or tests were weakened. Coverage variance across the two production-equivalent heads remains unexplained and is retained as an explicit limitation."
  "2026-10-24T13:34:09.125Z",codex-agent,"Failure-only LCOV diagnostics on CI 40098362665 identify both missing branches at index.ts:2773: resolvePreserveTimestamps short-circuit handling for the supported string false and string 0 values. Earlier 100% reports had not reliably exposed those untested alternatives. Extended the existing parser truth table for both camel and kebab option spellings with boolean and string enable/disable values. No production importer code changes; this replaces the earlier unexplained-variance limitation with direct coverage of the exact missing cases."
  "2026-10-24T13:35:53.296Z",codex-agent,"Coverage gap correction verified locally: node --test test/smoke.test.ts test/flag-declarations.test.ts via pm test --run --only-last --progress passes 117/117, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. The existing resolvePreserveTimestamps defaults-on/negation test now directly asserts both supported string false values and enabled values for both option aliases. build:test and release attestation verification pass. Ambient regressions and their byte-for-byte revert proof are unchanged. Releasing the claim for exact-head npm/Bun CI and orchestrator verification; item remains in_progress."
  "2026-10-24T15:34:47.359Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 design: snapshot receiver settings, template content and saved focus in the digest-bound plan. Persist a lease-protected transfer journal with per-source exact identity intents before creation and exact created item hashes before the after_create boundary. Resume reads only journal identities; changed settings refuse with plan_settings_changed until all rows have recorded creations. Revalidate item documents even for committed SDK chunk replay, reporting changed or missing items honestly without recreating them. Validate canonical records without a second destructive description normalization; seeded round-trip properties and every-row settings-drift interruption tests follow."
  "2026-10-24T15:42:32.983Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 identity behavioral revert proof: reverted only ownership, transferSteps and applyBeadsTransfer to the prior implementation, keeping snapshot-bound planning, round-trip validation and tests. Rebuilt successfully. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"prefix drift after the only created row\" test/transfer-properties.test.ts fails 0/1: after creating a, interruption and prefix change, replay produces 2 items instead of 1 while reporting success. Restored transfer.ts byte-for-byte, SHA256 e1ef620031118265e25b2c18f5cdfd91c482ad26e4cc21d274f6059c9e6f932e, and rebuilt."
  "2026-10-24T15:42:34.104Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 round-trip behavioral revert proof: reverted only toBead and validateBeadsTransferPlan to the previous second-pass description normalization, adapting solely the new settings argument. Identity journal fix and tests retained. Rebuild succeeds. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"plan round-trip\" test/transfer-properties.test.ts fails 0/2 with invalid_plan on generated saved plans (512 rows per seed, 23404582 and 12648430). Restored transfer.ts byte-for-byte at SHA256 e1ef620031118265e25b2c18f5cdfd91c482ad26e4cc21d274f6059c9e6f932e and rebuilt."
  "2026-10-24T15:43:54.219Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 verification: pm test --run --only-last --progress ran node --test test/transfer-properties.test.ts test/ambient-defaults.test.ts test/transfer.test.ts test/transfer-cli.test.ts test/reconcile.test.ts test/reconcile-cli.test.ts test/import-paths.test.ts; 106/106 pass, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. Includes actual SIGKILL recovery, 24 every-row interruption cases (three rows, four settings, chunk sizes 1 and 3), creation-to-ledger interruption, bootstrap and missing/corrupt ledger cases, edited/deleted pinned item replay, and two seeds 23404582/12648430 with 512 adversarial rows each (1024 total). Local transfer.ts V8 coverage is 100% lines/branches/functions. Typecheck, build, build:test, docstring lint (91 declarations across 12 sources) and whitespace checks pass; no separate lint script exists. Full unchanged npm and Bun release gates on Node 22 and 26 remain required CI evidence after push. Existing project policy disables linked-test result persistence; this comment retains the counts."
  "2026-10-24T15:48:19.677Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 full release evidence on implementation head 4c9fc77d1c1ee898f2fb8b7dc8ec5c0a1bfc1a05: CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/actions/runs/40108341218 passes npm run release:check and bun run release:check on both Node 22 and Node 26. Every gate passes 464/464 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, 100% measured lines/branches/functions across all 12 declared sources, and docstring lint 91/91 declarations. Four gates total 1856 test executions; unchanged scope and thresholds. Fresh tracker health, audit, packing, changelog, release attestation and Bun dependency-graph installation pass. CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/actions/runs/40108341231 passes. No new pm CLI/SDK defect found; pre-existing installer drift remains on pm-beads-v9r1. Claim is released, item stays in_progress for orchestrator verification, and no merge or release is performed. This evidence-only tracker commit will receive its own exact-head CI run."
  "2026-10-24T16:38:39.559Z",codex-agent,"Round 3: pulled remote head 6806409; origin/main is already contained. Replacing in-band source identity with registered bead_id metadata across transfer, import, export and reconciliation. Preserve source descriptions verbatim; recognize only the historical exact terminal marker when structured identity is absent and report first-touch migration. Extend both seeded 512-row cases through transfer, export and upsert, with independent behavioral revert proofs."
  "2026-10-24T16:44:26.059Z",codex-agent,"Implementation now uses registered bead_id metadata for transfer/import/reconciliation and structured export/upsert matching. Legacy decoding is limited to the exact old terminal envelope, disabled whenever metadata is present; migration removes only that envelope and reports via stderr plus history. New full-pipeline tests exposed an existing argv transport gap for NUL descriptions; importer now sends descriptions through the host stdin contract to preserve arbitrary bytes. Focused transfer/identity tests passed; updating legacy-format expectations and validating the two 512-row seeds."
  "2026-10-24T16:50:29.515Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 behavioral revert proofs (each changed function reverted alone, then restored): (1) reverted transfer createOptions to marker-based descriptions; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"structured identity wins\" test/identity.test.ts failed 0/1 because bead_id was absent. (2) restored broad legacy scanning in legacyBeadIdentity; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"legacy fallback\" test/identity.test.ts failed 0/1 on an embedded marker. Separately disabling first-touch migration failed the same test 0/1. (3) reverted only pmItemToBead to ignore structured identity; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"seed 23404582\" test/transfer-properties.test.ts failed 0/1 after transferring/exporting 512 rows, proving the pipeline catches an incorrect exported id. All changes restored; identity tests passed 3/3 before additional opt-out/error coverage was added. No thresholds changed."
  "2026-10-24T16:50:35.273Z",codex-agent,"Transport correction: the host stdin contract normalizes CRLF, so NUL and literal-dash descriptions now use public SDK mutations with preserveMutationStdinTokenFields; normal argv mutations preserve their existing behavior. An empty bead_id is persisted for identity opt-out and id-less imports, preventing new user-authored suffixes from being mistaken for legacy identity. Reconciliation migration disables unrelated extensions and refreshes the returned metadata after mutation."
  "2026-10-24T17:00:07.788Z",codex-agent,"Focused verification: node --test test/identity.test.ts executed through pm test --run --only-last --progress passes 5/5, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. Tests cover structured identity, exact legacy parsing and one-time reported migration, real import/export/upsert with NUL/CRLF/whitespace/literal dash, SDK validation/type fallback, and identity opt-out. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and whitespace checks pass. Full unchanged coverage and npm/Bun release evidence remain in progress. Local health retains existing installer fence drift and extension host/package version skew; no history repair or unrelated configuration change is applied."
  "2026-10-24T17:03:01.005Z",codex-agent,"Broader restored-source verification: node --test --experimental-test-coverage --test-coverage-include=identity.ts --test-coverage-include=index.ts --test-coverage-include=reconcile.ts --test-coverage-include=transfer.ts test/identity.test.ts test/import-paths.test.ts test/export-diff-paths.test.ts test/helper-truth-tables.test.ts test/ambient-defaults.test.ts test/smoke.test.ts test/transfer.test.ts test/reconcile.test.ts passes 257/257, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. Diagnostic coverage is 100% lines/branches/functions for identity.ts and reconciliation, and every newly introduced index.ts identity/transport branch is covered. This focused scope is not full-gate evidence; the unchanged full suite remains required on npm and Bun in CI. The seeded full pipeline retains two seeds with 512 rows each in a single receiving tracker per seed."
